  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A monochromatic light is incident at a certain angle on an equilateral triangular prism and suffers minimum deviation.\r\n\r\nIf the refractive index of the material of the prism is $\\sqrt{3}$,\r\n\r\nthen the angle of incidence is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MGr30",
      "text": "$90^{\\circ}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GxYC4",
      "text": "$30^{\\circ}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Y7mNa",
      "text": "$60^{\\circ}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OpHwI",
      "text": "$45^{\\circ}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For minimum deviation:\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{r}_{1}=\\mathrm{r}_{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{A}}{2}=30^{\\circ}$\r\n\r\nby Snell's law $\\mu_{1} \\sin \\mathrm{i}=\\mu_{2} \\sin \\mathrm{r}$\r\n\r\n$1 \\times \\sin i=\\sqrt{3} \\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Rightarrow i=60$",
    "image": null
  },
